# Two Major Areas of Computer Graphics

## 1. 2D Graphics

2D graphics deal with flat images.

Examples:

* icons
* text
* diagrams
* charts
* GUI elements

A 2D object usually has:

```
(x, y)
```

coordinates.

Example:

```
Screen

(0,0)
 +----------------+
 |                |
 |        *       |
 |                |
 +----------------+

        (x,y)
```

Operations include:

* drawing lines
* drawing circles
* rendering text
* image processing

---

## 2. 3D Graphics

3D graphics create objects with depth.

A point has:

```
(x, y, z)
```

coordinates.

Example:

```
        z
        |
        |
        +------ x
       /
      /
     y
```

Used in:

* games
* movies
* simulations
* VR

A 3D object:

```
       cube

        +------+
       /      /|
      +------+ |
      |      | +
      |      |/
      +------+
```

must be converted into a 2D image on the screen.

